# Small commits

Each finished slice gets its own commit before the next slice starts. A slice is one concern: layout, project metadata, one adapter, one plugin, or one test module.

## Message shape

Subject line, imperative, under 72 characters. It names the outcome. A blank line, then one or two sentences on why this slice exists. Mention what the slice deliberately leaves out when that boundary is the point.

```
Add the package layout around the Deep Agents harness.

The tree reserves the composition root, a CLI channel, and a plugin slot. No runtime behavior yet.
```

## What does not belong in one commit

- Layout and runtime behavior together
- A new adapter plus an unrelated plugin
- Config, dependencies, and tests for a feature that is not in the same slice
- Drive-by formatting or renames mixed with the change

## After the commit

Leave the working tree clean. In the reply, show the subject and body so the history stays readable one commit at a time.
